From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(OnScreenKeyboard): touches outside the keys reach the menu
 behind it

card_ui.tscn puts the keyboard in AlwaysVisibleContent, a MarginContainer,
which sizes it to the whole screen. Its root control passed mouse events
(MOUSE_FILTER_PASS), so while the keyboard was up it took every touch on the
screen, above the menu (z_index 21): a dialog's Submit button over the
keyboard could not be tapped, only reached with the controller (HW, MANGMI
Air X, 2026-10-23: Settings > Network's Wi-Fi password).

The root ignores mouse events now. The keys are buttons and the panel
behind them stops events itself, so the keyboard keeps every touch on it.

With taps reaching the menu, a tap on the field the keyboard types into
opens it again. Each open() emitted "opened", and the SpacerGrowerEffect
in card_ui.tscn grows the menu's KeyboardSpacer to its current height
plus the keyboard's, so every tap pushed the menu up by another keyboard
height (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-23). "opened" is emitted only when the
keyboard was closed; a second open() still takes the new target and
focuses the first key.

---
 core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.gd   | 7 +++++++
 core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.tscn | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.gd b/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.gd
index ba7453e..cfa2ba3 100644
--- a/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.gd
+++ b/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.gd
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@ enum MODE_SHIFT {
 @export var instance: KeyboardInstance = preload("res://core/global/keyboard_instance.tres")
 var _mode_shift: MODE_SHIFT = MODE_SHIFT.OFF
 var _last_input_focus: int
+## Between open() and close(). Another open() meanwhile (a tap on the field it types into) only
+## retargets: "opened" again grew the menu's keyboard spacer by the keyboard's height each time.
+var _is_open := false
 var logger := Log.get_logger("OSK", Log.LEVEL.INFO)
 
 @onready var rows_container := $%KeyboardRowsContainer as VBoxContainer
@@ -206,11 +209,15 @@ func open() -> void:
 			var overlay_window_id := ogui_windows[0]
 			xwayland.set_input_focus(overlay_window_id, 2)
 
+	if _is_open:
+		return
+	_is_open = true
 	opened.emit()
 
 
 # Closes the OSK
 func close() -> void:
+	_is_open = false
 	# Remove the OSK state
 	popup_state_machine.remove_state(osk_state)
 
diff --git a/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.tscn b/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.tscn
index ed25ec6..06e7d30 100644
--- a/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.tscn
+++ b/core/ui/common/osk/on_screen_keyboard.tscn
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ anchor_right = 1.0
 anchor_bottom = 1.0
 grow_horizontal = 2
 grow_vertical = 0
-mouse_filter = 1
+mouse_filter = 2
 script = ExtResource("1_3r64j")
 layout = ExtResource("2_0han2")
 
